{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Boundary Doctor"},"description":"Purpose: check a user-supplied red-line boundary before treating it as the site geometry. When to use: run after receiving a GeoJSON Polygon or MultiPolygon, especially before Site Verdict or focused constraint checks. Returns: closure, CRS, coordinate-range, topology, vertex-limit, and area checks; a stable boundary ID; calculated area; visible warnings; and an updated site_ref with red_line_upload confidence only when every blocking check passes. Limitations: V1 accepts EPSG:4326, OGC:CRS84, EPSG:27700, and EPSG:2157; it checks geometry but does not confirm title, ownership, survey accuracy, or a planning conclusion; it does not persist the uploaded geometry. Parameter guidance: pass the GeoJSON Feature or geometry in boundary_geojson, explicitly declare source_crs, optionally provide declared_area_m2 for a mismatch check, and pass an earlier site_ref to retain its address, LPA, and project context. Chaining: every response returns site_ref; pass it unchanged into another Atlasly tool to reuse the canonical site, coordinates, boundary confidence, LPA, evidence links, and project context.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"boundary_geojson":{"description":"GeoJSON Polygon, MultiPolygon, or Feature containing one. Coordinate order must match source_crs."},"declared_area_m2":{"description":"Optional area stated by the source, in square metres, for comparison with the coordinate-derived area","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":1000000000,"type":"number"},"site_ref":{"description":"Canonical site_ref returned by any previous Atlasly tool. Pass it unchanged to chain the same resolved site into this call; address, search_area, or project_id will be filled from it when omitted.","properties":{"address_aliases":{"items":{"maxLength":300,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"maxItems":4,"